# OSINT Investigation & Intelligence Report

A beginner-friendly passive OSINT investigation of the OWASP Foundation using publicly available information.

## 🎯 Project Objective

The goal of this project was to practice Open-Source Intelligence (OSINT) techniques and learn how to collect, verify, interpret, and document publicly available information ethically.

## 🔎 Target

**Organization:** OWASP Foundation  
**Domain:** `owasp.org`

**Investigation Type:** Passive OSINT

## 🛠️ Techniques Used

- Search-engine intelligence
- Google search operators
- Username/account investigation
- Public email investigation
- DNS enumeration
- A record analysis
- MX record analysis
- NS record analysis
- TXT/SPF analysis
- Reverse DNS investigation
- IP and ASN intelligence
- Public reputation research

## 📌 Key Findings

### Search Intelligence

Used search operators including:

```text
site:owasp.org
site:owasp.org "OWASP Foundation"
site:owasp.org filetype:pdf
```

These searches identified publicly indexed OWASP content and documents.

### DNS Intelligence

The domain resolved to:

```text
216.150.1.1
216.150.16.1
```

### Mail Infrastructure

MX records identified Google mail infrastructure for `owasp.org`.

### DNS Infrastructure

NS records identified Cloudflare nameservers:

```text
west.ns.cloudflare.com
fay.ns.cloudflare.com
```

### SPF

The domain published an SPF policy authorizing sending infrastructure associated with Google, Mailchimp, and Amazon SES.

### IP Intelligence

The investigated IP addresses were associated with cloud/hosting network infrastructure and AS16509.

Reverse DNS lookups did not return hostnames for the investigated IPs.

