## ⚖️ Ethical Considerations

This project used passive OSINT techniques and publicly available information only.

No:

- Unauthorized access
- Credential testing
- Exploitation
- Intrusive scanning
- Private-data collection
- Password collection
- Account compromise

was performed.

The investigation was conducted for educational and cybersecurity-learning purposes.

## 🧠 Skills Demonstrated

- Passive reconnaissance
- OSINT methodology
- Search-engine intelligence
- DNS analysis
- Email infrastructure analysis
- IP/ASN investigation
- Evidence collection
- Technical documentation
- Ethical cybersecurity research

## 🚀 Learning Outcome

This project helped develop a practical understanding of how publicly available information can be collected and correlated during an OSINT investigation.

It also reinforced the importance of verifying findings and avoiding unsupported conclusions when analyzing public infrastructure.

